                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game captures the spirit of classic 1990s point-and-click adventures:\n[list]\n    [*][b] Cartoonish world and eccentric characters [/b] - an alternate-history steampunk version of Central Europe. \n    [*][b] Absurd black comedy:[/b] the game prioritizes surreal humor and witty dialogue over taking its setting seriously.\n    [*][b] Classic point-and-click gameplay.[/b] Exploration, dialogue, and inventory puzzles form the core experience, with mini-games and action sequences providing occasional variety.\n    [*][b] Puzzle-focused progression.[/b] Most obstacles are solved through puzzles, though unlike many classic adventures, some can be completed in multiple ways (such as through different dialogue choices or optional puzzles).\n[/list] \n\nThat said, the game is certainly not for everyone:\n[list]\n    [*][b] Classic 'moon logic':[/b] as with many old-school adventure games, puzzle solutions can be unintuitive, favoring comedic payoff over realistic reasoning.\n    [*][b] Very niche political satire.[/b] Many jokes assume some knowledge of Central European history and the Austro-Hungarian Empire, though history enthusiasts are likely to appreciate them.\n    [*][b] Noticeably low-budget production:[/b] simple animations, static environments, limited voice acting, and reused assets. \n[/list]",
